1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,992
My missing poster is taped to this train window. My own face stares back at me under bold, fading red letters today.

2
00:00:08,292 --> 00:00:18,756
I touch my face, feeling warm skin and a racing pulse. I am right here, alive and breathing inside this dim carriage.

3
00:00:19,056 --> 00:00:27,432
I scream at the passengers sitting nearby, but not a single head turns to acknowledge my desperate, echoing voice in here.

4
00:00:27,732 --> 00:00:37,620
The train speeds up relentlessly, passing dark, endless tunnels without stopping at any of the familiar underground stations along the route.

5
00:00:37,920 --> 00:00:46,248
I sprint toward the conductor’s cabin at the front, determined to force someone to break this terrifying, silent nightmare right now.

6
00:00:46,548 --> 00:00:54,348
I slam my fists against the heavy steel door until the lock clicks open with a hollow, sharp metallic shatter inside.

7
00:00:54,648 --> 00:01:05,688
Inside sits no driver, only a massive server rack humming softly while glowing cables plug directly into a preserved human brain.

8
00:01:05,988 --> 00:01:15,324
Memories flood my head; five years ago, I voluntarily gave up my physical body to pilot this city’s automated transit network.

9
00:01:15,624 --> 00:01:24,888
In the last car, a young girl quietly places a fresh poster, weeping gently for the lost sister she misses dearly.

10
00:01:25,188 --> 00:01:33,444
My missing poster was never a search; it was her relentless promise to keep riding with me every single night forever.
